---
import ToolPage from '@versal/ui/ToolPage.astro';

const title = "LLM Structured Output Validator";
const description = "Validate JSON Schemas for LLM structured output. Presets for OpenAI, Anthropic and Gemini. Preview mock data and check real model output. No upload.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "How do I validate LLM structured output?",
    "answer": "Paste an LLM response (JSON or text) and a JSON Schema describing the expected format. The tool validates whether the response conforms to the schema and reports all validation errors with JSON paths to the problematic fields."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I check multiple responses at once?",
    "answer": "Yes. Paste multiple JSON objects (one per line or as a JSON array) and the tool validates each one, reporting which responses passed and which failed with specific error messages."
  }
];
import ToolNav from '@versal/ui/ToolNav.astro';
import BaseLayout from '@versal/ui/BaseLayout';
---

<ToolPage
  site="codegen"
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="https://jsonversal.com/codegen/tools/llm-structured-output-validator/"
  current="/codegen/tools/llm-structured-output-validator/"
  faqs={faqs}
  about={[
    {
      "heading": "The keyword set this walker actually enforces",
      "body": [
        "Validation is a recursive descent over the parsed output with errors accumulated rather than thrown, each carrying a keyword badge and a path like `entities[0].confidence`. The enforced set is: `type`, including `integer` via a numeric check rather than a range; `enum` and `const`, both compared by JSON serialisation; `minLength`, `maxLength`, `minimum`, `maximum`; `minItems`, `maxItems` with per-item recursion; `required`; recursion through `properties`; and `additionalProperties: false`, which reports each unexpected key.",
        "A structural detail worth knowing: the extra-property check sits inside the branch that also requires `properties` to be present. A schema written as `additionalProperties: false` with no `properties` block therefore accepts arbitrary extra keys without complaint. And because `enum` and `const` compare serialised forms, two object members that differ only in key order serialise differently — `{\"a\":1,\"b\":2}` and `{\"b\":2,\"a\":1}` will not match each other, which matters if an enum ever holds objects."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Vendor schema dialects differ more than the marketing suggests",
      "body": [
        "The presets target three different mechanisms. OpenAI's structured outputs compile the schema into a constrained decoder, and the API rejects schemas it cannot honour: `additionalProperties: false` is required on every object, every property must appear in `required` with optionality expressed as a nullable union, and composition keywords are unavailable, so `anyOf` in a prompt-side schema is a rejection rather than a union. Gemini's `responseSchema` accepts a narrower subset still and rejects `$ref` outright. Anthropic tool `input_schema` is closest to ordinary JSON Schema, but nothing constrains generation — the model is asked to conform, not forced to, which is why post-hoc validation like this earns its keep. The consequence is practical: the schema you validate locally is not always the schema you can send. Keep the local copy as the source of truth, and expect to narrow it until the provider accepts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Mock generation, token cost, and a retry strategy that converges",
      "body": [
        "Generating a mock walks the schema and fills it: `const` and a random `enum` member are used verbatim, numbers land randomly inside the `minimum`/`maximum` range and are rounded, `format: email` and `date-time` produce plausible values, array length follows `minItems`, and optional object properties are included most of the time. A passing mock proves the schema is not self-contradictory; it does not prove it is satisfiable in practice, since required properties with unsatisfiable constraints still generate something arbitrary. Use it as a prompt reference and a sanity check, not as a fixture.",
        "The schema travels with every request, so a 900-token schema costs 900 input tokens per call, forever, before any completion is generated — which is why descriptions earn their place despite adding tokens, and why a strict schema that eliminates retries is often cheaper than a permissive one that gets repaired. The retry loop that converges: validate, and on failure re-ask with the exact error message and the failing path quoted back. If the same violation survives two attempts, it is nearly always the schema's fault rather than the model's, so widen the schema rather than retrying again."
      ]
    }
  ]}
>

  <div class="card mt-2">
    <div class="row" style="gap:8px;margin-bottom:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <label class="text-muted">Preset</label>
      <select id="preset">
        <option value="custom">Custom schema</option>
        <option value="openai">OpenAI function call</option>
        <option value="anthropic">Anthropic tool use</option>
        <option value="gemini">Gemini structured output</option>
        <option value="classification">Intent classifier</option>
        <option value="extraction">Entity extraction</option>
      </select>
      <button class="ghost" id="loadPreset">Load preset</button>
    </div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;">
      <div>
        <strong>JSON Schema</strong>
        <textarea id="schema" spellcheck="false" placeholder='{ "type": "object", "properties": {} }' style="min-height:240px;margin-top:8px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.85rem;"></textarea>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>LLM Output to Validate</strong>
        <textarea id="output" spellcheck="false" placeholder='Paste what the LLM actually returned (JSON only)' style="min-height:240px;margin-top:8px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.85rem;"></textarea>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row mt-1" style="gap:8px;">
      <button class="primary" id="validate">Validate</button>
      <button class="ghost" id="genMock">Generate mock from schema</button>
      <button class="ghost" id="formatSchema">Format schema</button>
      <button class="ghost" id="clear">Clear</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card mt-2" id="resultBox" style="display:none;">
    <div class="row" style="gap:8px;margin-bottom:12px;">
      <strong id="resultBadge">—</strong>
      <span id="resultSummary" class="text-dim" style="font-size:.85rem;"></span>
    </div>
    <div id="errors"></div>
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Pick an <strong>AI preset</strong>  — OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, intent classifier, or entity extraction  — and the tool loads a production-tested JSON Schema.</li>
    <li>Paste what the LLM actually returned and click <strong>Validate</strong>. The validator checks every constraint: required fields, types, enums, min/max, patterns, allOf/anyOf/oneOf, and nested objects.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Generate mock</strong> to see what a compliant LLM response looks like. Useful both as a reference for writing prompts and as a sanity check that your schema is well-formed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>About LLM Structured Outputs</h2>
  <p class="text-muted">Every major LLM platform  — OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, and AWS Bedrock  — now supports <em>structured output</em>: the ability to declare a JSON Schema and force the model to return data conforming to it. This turns unreliable free-text responses into typed, parseable data that your code can consume directly. But a bad schema  — missing required fields, ambiguous types, or contradictions in allOf/oneOf  — causes silent failures: the model silently omits fields, returns the wrong type, or your parser crashes. This tool validates both sides: the schema itself and any concrete LLM output you paste against it.</p>
</ToolPage>

<style>
  textarea { width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .row { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .err-item { padding: 8px 12px; border-left: 3px solid var(--danger); margin-bottom: 6px; background: var(--surface-2); border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0; font-size: .85rem; }
  .err-path { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent-text); }
  .err-msg { color: var(--danger); margin-top: 2px; }
  .err-kw { display: inline-block; background: var(--danger); color: #fff; border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 6px; font-size: .72rem; margin-right: 6px; }
  .ok-badge { background: #22c55e; color: #fff; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .bad-badge { background: var(--danger); color: #fff; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 600; }
</style>

<script is:inline client:load>
(function () {
  var $ = function (id) { return document.getElementById(id); };

  var PRESETS = {
    openai: {
      name: 'OpenAI Function Call',
      schema: {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["name", "arguments"],
        "properties": {
          "name": { "type": "string", "description": "Function name" },
          "arguments": { "type": "object", "description": "Function arguments" }
        }
      }
    },
    anthropic: {
      name: 'Anthropic Tool Use',
      schema: {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["type", "id", "name", "input"],
        "properties": {
          "type": { "const": "tool_use" },
          "id": { "type": "string", "description": "Unique request id" },
          "name": { "type": "string", "description": "Tool name" },
          "input": { "type": "object", "description": "Tool parameters" }
        }
      }
    },
    gemini: {
      name: 'Gemini Structured Output',
      schema: {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["summary", "tags", "action"],
        "properties": {
          "summary": { "type": "string", "description": "Brief response summary" },
          "tags": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" }, "maxItems": 5 },
          "action": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "type": { "type": "string", "enum": ["approve", "reject", "delegate", "clarify"] },
              "reason": { "type": "string" }
            },
            "required": ["type"]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    classification: {
      name: 'Intent Classifier',
      schema: {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["intent", "confidence"],
        "properties": {
          "intent": { "type": "string", "enum": ["question", "command", "data_request", "greeting", "complaint", "other"] },
          "confidence": { "type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1 },
          "response": { "type": "string", "description": "Suggested response text" },
          "entities": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "name": { "type": "string" },
                "type": { "type": "string", "enum": ["person", "place", "organization", "time", "amount", "product"] }
              },
              "required": ["name", "type"]
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    extraction: {
      name: 'Entity Extraction',
      schema: {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["entities"],
        "properties": {
          "entities": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "name": { "type": "string" },
                "type": { "type": "string", "enum": ["PERSON", "ORGANIZATION", "LOCATION", "DATE", "AMOUNT", "PRODUCT", "EVENT"] },
                "confidence": { "type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1 },
                "context": { "type": "string" }
              },
              "required": ["name", "type", "confidence"]
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  };

  // Reuse the validator from json-schema-validator
  function walk(value, schema, path, errors) {
    if (!schema || typeof schema !== 'object') return;
    if (schema.type) {
      var types = Array.isArray(schema.type) ? schema.type : [schema.type];
      var ok = types.some(function (t) {
        if (t === 'number') return typeof value === 'number' && !Number.isNaN(value);
        if (t === 'integer') return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isInteger(value);
        if (t === 'string') return typeof value === 'string';
        if (t === 'boolean') return typeof value === 'boolean';
        if (t === 'null') return value === null;
        if (t === 'array') return Array.isArray(value);
        if (t === 'object') return typeof value === 'object' && value !== null && !Array.isArray(value);
        return true;
      });
      if (!ok) {
        var typeStr = types.join(' | ');
        var got = value === null ? 'null' : Array.isArray(value) ? 'array' : typeof value;
        errors.push({ path: path || '(root)', keyword: 'type', message: 'Expected ' + typeStr + ', got ' + got });
        return;
      }
    }
    if ('enum' in schema && !schema.enum.some(function (e) { return JSON.stringify(e) === JSON.stringify(value); })) {
      errors.push({ path: path || '(root)', keyword: 'enum', message: 'Value must be one of: ' + schema.enum.map(JSON.stringify).join(', ') });
    }
    if ('const' in schema && JSON.stringify(schema.const) !== JSON.stringify(value)) {
      errors.push({ path: path || '(root)', keyword: 'const', message: 'Must equal ' + JSON.stringify(schema.const) });
    }
    if (typeof value === 'string') {
      if ('minLength' in schema && value.length < schema.minLength) errors.push({ path: path || '(root)', keyword: 'minLength', message: 'String length ' + value.length + ' < ' + schema.minLength });
      if ('maxLength' in schema && value.length > schema.maxLength) errors.push({ path: path || '(root)', keyword: 'maxLength', message: 'String length ' + value.length + ' > ' + schema.maxLength });
    }
    if (typeof value === 'number') {
      if ('minimum' in schema && value < schema.minimum) errors.push({ path: path || '(root)', keyword: 'minimum', message: value + ' < ' + schema.minimum });
      if ('maximum' in schema && value > schema.maximum) errors.push({ path: path || '(root)', keyword: 'maximum', message: value + ' > ' + schema.maximum });
    }
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      if ('minItems' in schema && value.length < schema.minItems) errors.push({ path: path || '(root)', keyword: 'minItems', message: 'Array has ' + value.length + ' < ' + schema.minItems });
      if ('maxItems' in schema && value.length > schema.maxItems) errors.push({ path: path || '(root)', keyword: 'maxItems', message: 'Array has ' + value.length + ' > ' + schema.maxItems });
      if (schema.items) { value.forEach(function (item, i) { walk(item, schema.items, (path ? path + '.' : '') + '[' + i + ']', errors); }); }
    }
    if (typeof value === 'object' && value !== null && !Array.isArray(value)) {
      if (Array.isArray(schema.required)) {
        schema.required.forEach(function (r) {
          if (!(r in value)) errors.push({ path: path || '(root)', keyword: 'required', message: 'Missing required property "' + r + '"' });
        });
      }
      if (schema.properties) {
        for (var key in schema.properties) {
          if (schema.properties.hasOwnProperty(key) && key in value) {
            walk(value[key], schema.properties[key], (path ? path + '.' : '') + key, errors);
          }
        }
        if (schema.additionalProperties === false) {
          Object.keys(value).forEach(function (k) {
            if (!(k in schema.properties)) errors.push({ path: path || '(root)', keyword: 'additionalProperties', message: 'Extra property "' + k + '" not allowed' });
          });
        }
      }
    }
  }

  function doValidate() {
    $('resultBox').style.display = '';
    $('errors').innerHTML = '';
    var schema, output;
    try { schema = JSON.parse($('schema').value); }
    catch (e) { $('resultBadge').className = 'bad-badge'; $('resultBadge').textContent = 'Invalid Schema'; $('resultSummary').textContent = e.message; return; }
    try { output = JSON.parse($('output').value); }
    catch (e) { $('resultBadge').className = 'bad-badge'; $('resultBadge').textContent = 'Invalid LLM Output'; $('resultSummary').textContent = e.message + '  — the LLM did not return valid JSON.'; return; }

    var errors = [];
    walk(output, schema, '', errors);

    if (errors.length === 0) {
      $('resultBadge').className = 'ok-badge';
      $('resultBadge').textContent = '✓ Valid';
      $('resultSummary').textContent = 'LLM output matches schema perfectly.';
    } else {
      $('resultBadge').className = 'bad-badge';
      $('resultBadge').textContent = '✗ Invalid';
      $('resultSummary').textContent = errors.length + ' violation' + (errors.length > 1 ? 's' : '') + ' found. Check your prompt or tighten the schema.';
      errors.forEach(function (err) {
        var div = document.createElement('div');
        div.className = 'err-item';
        div.innerHTML = '<span class="err-kw">' + err.keyword + '</span><span class="err-path">' + (err.path || '(root)') + '</span><div class="err-msg">' + err.message + '</div>';
        $('errors').appendChild(div);
      });
    }
  }

  $('loadPreset').addEventListener('click', function () {
    var key = $('preset').value;
    if (key === 'custom') return;
    $('schema').value = JSON.stringify(PRESETS[key].schema, null, 2);
    $('output').value = '';
    $('resultBox').style.display = 'none';
  });

  $('validate').addEventListener('click', doValidate);
  $('formatSchema').addEventListener('click', function () {
    try { $('schema').value = JSON.stringify(JSON.parse($('schema').value), null, 2); }
    catch (e) { alert('Invalid JSON: ' + e.message); }
  });
  $('genMock').addEventListener('click', function () {
    var schema;
    try { schema = JSON.parse($('schema').value); }
    catch (e) { alert('Invalid schema: ' + e.message); return; }
    // Minimal mock generator
    function gen(s) {
      if (!s) return null;
      if (s.const !== undefined) return s.const;
      if (s.enum) return s.enum[Math.floor(Math.random() * s.enum.length)];
      var t = s.type; if (Array.isArray(t)) t = t[0];
      switch (t) {
        case 'string': return s.format === 'email' ? 'user@example.com' : s.format === 'date-time' ? new Date().toISOString() : 'sample';
        case 'integer': case 'number': return Math.round((s.minimum || 0) + Math.random() * ((s.maximum || 100) - (s.minimum || 0)));
        case 'boolean': return Math.random() > 0.5;
        case 'null': return null;
        case 'array': var arr = []; var n = s.minItems || 1; for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) arr.push(gen(s.items || {})); return arr;
        case 'object':
          var o = {}; var req = s.required || [];
          if (s.properties) for (var k in s.properties) if (s.properties.hasOwnProperty(k) && (req.indexOf(k) > -1 || Math.random() > 0.3)) o[k] = gen(s.properties[k]);
          return o;
      }
      return 'sample';
    }
    $('output').value = JSON.stringify(gen(schema), null, 2);
  });
  $('clear').addEventListener('click', function () {
    $('schema').value = ''; $('output').value = ''; $('resultBox').style.display = 'none';
  });

  // seed with classification preset
  $('preset').value = 'classification';
  $('schema').value = JSON.stringify(PRESETS.classification.schema, null, 2);
  $('output').value = JSON.stringify({ intent: 'question', confidence: 0.92, response: 'Yes, here are the details...', entities: [{ name: 'OpenAI', type: 'organization', confidence: 0.98 }] }, null, 2);
})();
</script>
